From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charcoal maintainers <charcoal@localhost>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 16:10:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] zram: complete ZRAM-IR 1.3 incompressible call port

The SteamOS 6.16 zram write path retains one legacy three-argument call
to write_incompressible_page().  ZRAM-IR 1.3 extends that helper with
compressor priority and incompressibility state.  Pass the primary
compressor priority for this legacy primary-compressor fallback, and
only mark the slot incompressible when there are no additional active
compressors that could still be attempted.

This is a compatibility completion for the ZRAM-IR 1.3 port; it does not
remove or disable any upstream ZRAM-IR functionality.

---
 drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c b/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c
--- a/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/block/zram/zram_drv.c
@@ -1896,7 +1896,8 @@ static int zram_write_page(struct zram *zram, struct page *page, u32 index)
 
 	if (comp_len >= huge_class_size) {
 		zcomp_stream_put(zstrm);
-		return write_incompressible_page(zram, page, index);
+		return write_incompressible_page(zram, page, index, ZRAM_PRIMARY_COMP,
+						       zram->num_active_comps <= 1);
 	}
 
 	handle = zs_malloc(zram->mem_pool, comp_len,
-- 
